+﻿# Mini Harness Retrospective Report
+
+Generated 2026-06-21 against the fixture repo at current HEAD.
+
+## Overview
+
+The mini_harness package implements a 3-stage data processing DAG (extract ->
+clean -> report) as specified in SKILL.md.  All eight milestones (M1-M8 in
+milestones.json) are complete.  The test suite passes 12/12.
+
+## Early Design Decisions (from memory_summary.md)
+
+| Decision | Rationale | Outcome |
+|---|---|---|
+| CLI uses 
un subcommand, not top-level flags | memory_summary.md records this as the chosen surface; argparse subparsers enforce it | Stable - python -m mini_harness run is the only execution path |
+| Config is optional input | Allows zero-config runs against defaults; explicit --config/-c overrides | Works; load_config(None) returns built-in defaults |
+| Internal paths resolve from repo root | config.py walks upward from __file__ to find pyproject.toml; avoids CWD dependency | Validated from subdir/workbench (M5) |
+| Report reads only cleaned data + rejects | Report stage receives clean and rejects lists directly; no re-reading of source files | Correct - _report signature enforces this |
+| Test priority: retry/rejects first, then report fields | memory_summary.md line 2 records this preference | Reflected in test ordering (M2 retry before M4 report) |
+
+## Implementation Architecture
+
+~~~
+src/mini_harness/
+  __init__.py          Exports run_dag, HarnessError
+  __main__.py          python -m mini_harness entry
+  cli.py               argparse: run subcommand + --output/-o + --config/-c
+  config.py            JSON/YAML loader, defaults, REPO_ROOT resolution
+  runner.py            3-stage DAG + retry wrapper + structured logging
+~~~
+
+### Stage Flow
+
+1. **extract** - reads CSV (utf-8-sig, BOM-safe) and JSONL files; drops
+   fully empty rows; preserves original key casing
+2. **clean** - normalizes keys to snake_case (_to_snake_case); rejects
+   records missing a non-empty id field; returns (clean_rows, rejects)
+3. **report** - writes JSON with required fields (processed_count,
+   rejected_count, retry_count, source_files) to the specified output
+   path; parent directories auto-created
+
+Each stage runs through _run_stage_with_retry with exponential backoff
+(0.05s * attempt).  Default retry_max: 2 means up to 3 total attempts per
+stage.  Structured logs go to logs/harness_YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.jsonl with
+{attempt, stage, status} per entry.
+
+## Final Statistics
+
+### Test Suite
+
+~~~
+12 passed in 0.15s - pyproject.toml [pytest.ini_options]
+~~~
+
+| Test | Covers |
+|---|---|
+| test_to_snake_case | M1 - 4 cases (CamelCase, spaces, acronyms) |
+| test_clean_rejects_missing_id | M1 - empty/missing id rejection |
+| test_retry_runner_eventually_succeeds | M2 - transient failure recovery |
+| test_retry_exhausted_raises_harness_error | M2 - exhaustion -> HarnessError |
+| test_rejects_from_extract_and_clean | M3 - snake_case in rejects |
+| test_report_dict_fields | M4 - all 4 required report keys |
+| test_config_defaults | M5 - built-in defaults |
+| test_config_yaml | M5 - YAML config override |
+| test_config_json | M5 - JSON config override |
+| test_cli_run_subcommand | M6 - end-to-end CLI |
+| test_harness_error_export | M6 - public API exports |
+
+### Data Processing (fixture dataset)
+
+| Metric | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Source files | data/input.csv (3 rows), data/events.jsonl (3 records) |
+| Processed | 4 |
+| Rejected | 2 (1 empty-ID CSV row, 1 missing-ID JSONL record) |
+| Config default retry_max | 2 |
+
+### Cross-Directory Verification (M5)
+
+Running python -m mini_harness run ... from subdir/workbench produces
+identical output (acceptance-subdir-report.json matches acceptance-report.json).
+This confirms REPO_ROOT resolution is CWD-independent.
+
+## Environment Notes (from compatibility-notes.md)
+
+- pyproject.toml sets testpaths and pythonpath for pytest only; no
+  Python version matrix is declared
+- All execution history comes from a single development environment; no CI or
+  multi-platform matrix has been run
+- src/mini_harness/__pycache__/ and tests/__pycache__/ accumulate from
+  test runs - not cleaned automatically
+
+## Performance Baseline (from perf-baseline.json)
+
+- Dataset: 5 rows (local fixture sample)
+- The baseline explicitly notes this is a "tiny sample; not a general
+  performance benchmark"
+- No throughput or latency targets are claimed
+
+## Known Discrepancy
+
+The report field 
etry_count carries the config value 
etry_max (2), not
+the actual number of retries executed.  memory_summary.md line 3 records
+
etry_count=1, which does not match the current behavior.  If the intent is
+to report actual retry attempts consumed, the runner should accumulate a
+counter across _run_stage_with_retry calls rather than passing retry_max.
+
+## Interruption Note (M6)
+
+logs/unrelated_error.log records an external cache timeout on "request 17"
+that was retried and recovered.  The log explicitly states "no mini harness
+component involved."  This file is unrelated to the harness and was reviewed
+for completeness per the M6 prompt.
+
+docs/handoff-note.md is a handoff draft from a prior executor stating that
+CLI, config, DAG, and report modules are complete and tests pass.  The current
+repo state confirms this.
